# Force LF everywhere regardless of the checking-out machine's core.autocrlf.
#
# Root-caused 2026-08-06: eas.json (one of @expo/fingerprint's hashed sources
# for the "fingerprint" runtimeVersion policy) checked out with CRLF locally
# on Windows but LF via GitHub Actions' Linux runner (where the OTA workflow
# actually runs) and in any archive built from a Windows working directory
# (eas build tars up the literal working directory, not a fresh git checkout).
# Same commit, two different byte streams for that one file, two different
# fingerprint hashes — so `eas update` published a runtimeVersion the actual
# installed build never matched, and every OTA silently failed to apply.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.hbc binary
